    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0160" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.50/4–2646: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rankin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-04-26T10:00:00+02:00">April 26, 1946—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 27—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>563. Letter dated April 25 from Minister Coordination Stephanopoulos approves
                    sending three experts suggested Deptel 480, April 12<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d95-f1"/> and expresses gratitude US action.</p>
                <p>Request Dept telegraph names when selected and clarify points raised Embtel 539,
                    April 21,<anchor n="91" xml:id="d95-f2"/> second paragraph, to avoid possible
                    misunderstanding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rankin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="90" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it expressed the Department’s belief that the Greek request for the
                    sending of American economic experts should be confirmed by the new Greek
                    Government (868.50/3–646).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d95-f2" n="91" xml:id="d95-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
